94: * A staged header wins over the same header set by the handler, so a miss looks the same as a hit.
95: *
96: * Headers that decide whether a response may be stored stay visible to the cache: a staged `Cache-Control` and every staged `Vary` name except `origin`. A response that middleware marked `private`/`no-store`, or that varies on a request header the cache isn't keyed on, is therefore not stored. A staged `private`/`no-store` `Cache-Control` is also sent to the client in place of the one the cached handler sets, so a CDN in front of the app doesn't store it either. A `Vary: Origin` is isolated, because the CORS headers it declares are staged per request as well.
97: *
98: * Properties of the wrapped handler (such as ocache's `invalidate`, `expire` and `resolveKeys`) are copied to the returned handler.
